  "facts": [
    "The Hadsel Bridge, a 1,011‑metre cantilever marvel opened in 1978, spans the Langøysundet strait, linking the islands of Langøya and Børøya with a main 150‑metre span and 30‑metre sea clearance.",
    "Built as part of a 1970s island‑connecting push, the Hadsel Bridge joined forces with the Sortland, Andøy, and Kvalsaukan bridges to knit Vesterålen’s islands into a single road network.",
    "Initially a toll bridge, the Hadsel Bridge today offers free passage, a change that has eased travel between the town of Stokmarknes on Hadseløya and neighboring Langøya."
